  "question": {
    "text": "Among the following allotropic forms of sulphur, the number of allotropic forms, which will show paramagnetism is _______.<br />(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></math>-sulphur<br />(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#946;</mi></math>-sulphur<br />(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>-form"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>-sulphur and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>-sulphur are diamagnetic. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>-form is paramagnetic."
  }
